Linux system libraries (LGPL) — written offer
================================================================================

On Linux, Conduit links against GTK 3, GLib, libsoup, and WebKitGTK, which are
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL-2.1-or-later or
LGPL-2.0-or-later, depending on component).

The .deb package links these dynamically against distribution-provided copies;
they are System Libraries under GPL-3.0 section 1 and are not redistributed by
this project.

The AppImage bundle DOES include copies of these libraries. Because that
constitutes conveying LGPL-licensed works, the following applies to AppImage
distributions:

  - The LGPL libraries are dynamically linked within the bundle, so recipients
    may replace them with modified versions and relink, as required by
    LGPL-2.1 section 6(a) / LGPL-3.0 section 4(d)(1).

  - Source code for these libraries is available from their upstream projects:
      GTK 3      https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gtk
      GLib       https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/glib
      libsoup    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libsoup
      WebKitGTK  https://webkitgtk.org/

    On request, the copyright holder will provide the complete corresponding
    source for the specific versions included in any AppImage released by this
    project. Open an issue at the repository to request it.

On macOS, Conduit uses the system WKWebView framework. On Windows, it uses the
Microsoft Edge WebView2 runtime, installed separately via the download
bootstrapper and not redistributed with the application. Both are System
Libraries under GPL-3.0 section 1.
